          "message": {
            "text": "jail escape via alias expansion (prefix substitution, case folding, alias to host path) — No issue identified: src/diraliases.c + docwd() alias fallback (CWD, SITE ALIAS)\n\nAlias data comes only from ALIASES_FILE (CONFDIR, root-owned, parsed once at startup by init_aliases()); no client input reaches the alias table. lookup_alias() is an exact strcmp — no prefix/case-insensitive matching, so \"alias/src\" or \"ALIAS\" do not select an alias. Live test with `aliasin=/inside/` and `aliasout=<host>/outside/`: `CWD aliasin` resolved to /inside inside the jail, `CWD aliasout` failed (the absolute host path is re-based by chroot()/fakexlate()), and `CWD` never returned an out-of-jail path. The alias chdir target skips checknamesanity(), but it is still subject to the kernel chroot / fakexlate rewrite on every path, and the value is operator-controlled configuration."
          },
