          "ruleId": "strix-coverage/canonicalisation-bypass-oob-read-in-built-in-realpath",
          "ruleIndex": 18,
          "kind": "notApplicable",
          "level": "none",
          "message": {
            "text": "canonicalisation bypass / OOB read in built-in realpath — Not applicable: src/bsd-realpath.c bsd_realpath()\n\nbsd-realpath.c is only compiled when !HAVE_REALPATH || USE_BUILTIN_REALPATH; on glibc -DHAVE_REALPATH=1 makes the platform realpath() the compiled-in one (verified by building both ways). Its only caller in the daemon is displayrate() (src/ftpd.c:2803) for the upload-script/altlog path after a transfer completes — it never gates a filesystem operation, so a failure there only aborts the log entry. Latent nit noted for completeness: the dead `else if (slen == 0)` branch inside `if (slen < 0 || slen >= sizeof symlink)` leaves slen==0 reaching `symlink[slen - 1]` (bsd-realpath.c:269), a one-byte stack read; Linux cannot create a symlink with an empty target (symlink(\"\") fails ENOENT) and readlink() on a valid link returns >= 1, so it is unreachable."
          },
          "locations": [
