            "text": "jail escape for anonymous sessions (ANON_DIR setup path) — No issue identified: douser() anonymous jail setup + anonymous path commands\n\nLive anonymous session against a --with-virtualchroot build (ANON_DIR jail, dot_read_anon=0): `RETR ../afile.txt`, `../../afile.txt`, `/afile.txt`, `/etc/passwd` and `../../../ftproot_sibling/sib.txt` all resolved inside the jail or returned 550; `CWD ..`, `../..`, `/` clamp to `/`; `STOR ../up.txt` created the file at the jail root (verified on disk as <jail>/up.txt) and not outside; MKD/DELE/CHMOD are refused by the anonymous policy in dodele/domkd/dochmod before any filesystem call. The anonymous chroot setup path (douser(): chdir(pw_dir) || chroot(pw_dir) || chdir(\"/\")) therefore leaves the same controls in place as the virtual-user path."
