          "message": {
            "text": "Quota bypass / malformed quota file reset to zero / integer overflow — Ruled out: src/quotas.c quota_update (.ftpquota parsing, files/size accounting, locking)\n\nA quota'd user cannot touch /.ftpquota: checknamesanity() rejects any name containing QUOTA_FILE (src/ftpd.c:786-791) on every mutating command; verified 553 for STOR/APPE/DELE/MKD/RMD/RNFR/CHMOD/UTIME/MFMT including /, ./, suffix and upper-case variants. File is 0600 owned by session uid. Accounting verified live against the built daemon (exact limit accepted, +1 byte rejected and rolled back, aborted RST upload accounted, delete/rename/mkdir/rmdir consistent). Fail-open on a malformed file is real but needs a local writer who can already write the user's files directly, so no privilege boundary is crossed; wrapping of stored values near 2^64 is unreachable from the daemon path."
