        {
          "ruleId": "strix-coverage/forged-scoreboard-entry-causing-privileged-action-format-string-buffer-issues",
          "ruleIndex": 24,
          "kind": "pass",
          "level": "none",
          "message": {
            "text": "Forged scoreboard entry causing privileged action / format-string / buffer issues — Ruled out: src/ftpwho-update.c + src/pure-ftpwho.c scoreboard write/read (root helper)\n\nScoreboard dir is created/hardened to root-owned 0700 (ftpwho-update.c:108-130); entries are opened O_NOFOLLOW and required to be regular, uid 0, mode 0600 and exactly sizeof(FTPWhoEntry) (pure-ftpwho.c:841-854) before parsing, so a non-root local user or FTP client cannot inject an entry; pure-ftpwho refuses to run unless euid is 0 (737-742) and unlinks only names starting with `client-` that fail kill(pid,0). Attacker-controlled filename/account strings go through xml_escaped/shell_escaped, and control characters (incl. ESC) are rejected at upload time by ISCTRLCODE in checknamesanity, so no terminal/HTML injection via filenames."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "logicalLocations": [
