          "message": {
            "text": "LDAP injection, ambiguous multi-entry result, anonymous-bind regression — Ruled out: src/log_ldap.c filter/DN construction and credential check\n\nStatic trace (LDAP back end is not buildable here: no ldap.h dev headers, requires --with-ldap). The username reaches LDAP only after pw_ldap_validate_name (src/log_ldap.c:319-336) which allows only a-zA-Z0-9 space - @ _ ' . and rejects `*`, `(`, `)`, `\\` and control characters, so filter injection is impossible; the filter itself is a config template where '%' is refused and only `\\L` becomes `%s`, and snprintf is size-checked (log_ldap.c:250-264). The ChangeLog 1.0.54 multi-entry claim is present and correct: ldap_count_entries != 1 rejects ambiguous results with a warning (log_ldap.c:271-284). Anonymous bind is intact for a NULL binddn (pwd set NULL, ldap_bind_s(NULL,NULL)) at log_ldap.c:163-165 and 225."
