          "message": {
            "text": "Privilege escalation / uid 0 selection via virtual-user record — Ruled out: src/log_puredb.c pw_puredb_parseline uid/gid validation (PureDB record -> process identity)\n\nControl: after `result->uid = (uid_t) strtoul(line,&endptr,10)` the check `line==endptr || *endptr!=0` rejects non-numeric/partial fields and `if (result->uid <= (uid_t)0 || result->gid <= (gid_t)0) return -1` (log_puredb.c:321-336, #ifndef ACCEPT_ROOT_VIRTUAL_USERS) runs on the post-truncation value, so every string that truncates to 0 is rejected. Verified dynamically both in-process (harness linking the real log_puredb.c + puredb_read.c) and over FTP against a locally built daemon: uid '0','00','0000',' 0','0 ','+0','-0','0x0','4294967296' and gid '0',' 0','4294967296' all -> auth_ok=-1 / 530; control record uid 1000 logs in and the file it uploads is owned 1000:1000, proving the identity that is actually applied. ACCEPT_ROOT_VIRTUAL_USERS is never defined by configure.ac, so the default build always enforces this."
          },
