          "ruleIndex": 31,
          "kind": "pass",
          "level": "none",
          "message": {
            "text": "Out-of-bounds read/write on corrupted or hostile PureDB file — No issue identified: puredb/src/puredb_read.c puredb_open/puredb_find/puredb_read on malformed databases\n\nFuzzed the real puredb_read.c under ASan/UBSan: 8000 iterations of 1-8 random byte mutations plus truncation on a 337 KB database, calling puredb_find_s for several keys and puredb_read on hits -> no out-of-bounds access. Bounds checks are effective at each dereference: read_be_long (offset > db->size-4), read_memcmp (len > db->size-offset), the key_size/data_size window checks in puredb_find, and the `offset/len` clamp in puredb_read. Only defect found is a signed left-shift UB at puredb_read.c:69 (`mapoffset[0] << 24` on int) which UBSan reports but which has no memory-safety consequence. Note the DB is root-owned data, so this class is not remotely reachable."
