          "ruleId": "strix-coverage/ip-allow-deny-acl-bypass-malformed-cidr-failing-open",
          "ruleIndex": 32,
          "kind": "pass",
          "level": "none",
          "message": {
            "text": "IP allow/deny ACL bypass, malformed CIDR failing open — Ruled out: src/log_puredb.c access_ip_match/access_ip_check (per-user client and local IP rules)\n\nTested over FTP from two distinct peer addresses (127.0.0.1 and the container's 172.17.0.2) with records built by mkdb_raw so each field is unambiguous: exact /32 allow, foreign /8 allow, deny-only, allow+deny, /31 pair, 0.0.0.0/1 mask arithmetic, comma lists, hostname rule (A record), and invalid widths (/33, /0, /-1) all behaved as documented, with invalid widths and unparsable allow patterns denying. Positive and negative controls differed (allow=127.0.0.1 -> 230 from 127.0.0.1, 530 from 172.17.0.2; allow=172.17.0.2 -> the inverse). access_ip_check is fail-closed: with a non-empty allow list a non-match returns -1, and a malformed CIDR returns -1 from access_ip_match which is also treated as deny."
          },
