        {
          "ruleId": "strix-coverage/ipv6-cidr-rules-silently-dropped-acl-bypass",
          "ruleIndex": 33,
          "kind": "pass",
          "level": "none",
          "message": {
            "text": "IPv6 CIDR rules silently dropped -> ACL bypass — Ruled out: src/log_puredb.c IPv6 CIDR matching (access_ip_match inet_pton/ipv6_cidr_match branch) and IPv6 rules as stored by pure-pw\n\nSecurity outcome is fail-closed in every variant I could construct: '::1/128', '::/0', '2001:db8::/32', '::ffff:1.2.3.4' written into any of the four IP fields all shift the record because ':' is PW_LINE_SEP; the truncated first token always lands in a position that either fails access_ip_match (no CIDR, no inet_pton, no resolution -> deny) or leaves garbage in the time field, which time_restrictions_check rejects (sscanf \"%u-%u\" != 2 -> return -1). Verified end-to-end: pure-pw useradd -r '::1/128' produced an empty \"Allowed client IPs\" field plus a stray \"1/128\" time field, and the account was denied from both 127.0.0.1 and ::1. The hostname path (which is the only way an IPv6 comparison actually runs) works correctly: allow=localhost matches a ::1 client (230) and denies 172.17.0.2 (530), while IPv4-only rules deny a v6 peer. Defect recorded as an observation for the parent: IPv6 CIDR patterns cannot be represented in the record format at all (pure-pw does not escape ':' in -r/-R/-i/-I), so the ChangeLog's \"IP access rules now support IPv6 patterns\" is unusable and self-locks the account rather than weakening it."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "logicalLocations": [
                {
                  "fullyQualifiedName": "src/log_puredb.c IPv6 CIDR matching (access_ip_match inet_pton/ipv6_cidr_match branch) and IPv6 rules as stored by pure-pw"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "properties": {
            "strix": {
              "coverage_outcome": "ruled_out",
              "risk_area": "IPv6 CIDR rules silently dropped -> ACL bypass",
              "surface": "src/log_puredb.c IPv6 CIDR matching (access_ip_match inet_pton/ipv6_cidr_match branch) and IPv6 rules as stored by pure-pw",
              "recorded_by": "PureDB And Auth Auditor",
              "source": "agent_reported"
            }
          }
        },
