          "kind": "pass",
          "level": "none",
          "message": {
            "text": "Writing uid 0 / separator-injected records via the admin tool; offset overflow in the DB writer — No issue identified: src/pure-pw.c useradd/usermod/passwd/mkdb field validation + puredb/src/puredb_write.c\n\nVerified end-to-end with the built pure-pw + daemon: useradd/mkdb/puredb-read chain authenticates a bcrypt record (auth_ok=1) and rejects a wrong password. do_useradd rejects uid/gid <= 0 before writing (pure-pw.c:848-853) and parse_pw_line rejects them when reading back (405-411); filter_pw_line_sep scrubs ':' from login/gecos/home so a login cannot inject extra fields. puredbw_add's size/offset checks (puredb_write.c:93-125) keep the merged file under 4 GiB so the u32 offsets cannot overflow. Observed defects (no privilege gain, recorded for the parent): out-of-range numeric fields are silently truncated on read (uid '4294967297' -> uid 1 was accepted and an uploaded file was owned by uid 1; '4294976296' -> uid 9000; values > 2^64 -> (uid_t)-1 -> setuid fails and the session is killed without a reply), and ':' in -r/-R/-i/-I is not escaped (see the IPv6 coverage entry)."
          },
