            "text": "PAM authentication bypass / auth_ok mishandling — Requires further review: src/log_pam.c pw_pam_check (PAM backend, USE_PAM build)\n\nStatic review only: libpam headers and pam modules are not installed in the sandbox, so the USE_PAM build could not be produced. Read of log_pam.c:144-221 shows the success path requires pam_authenticate()==PAM_SUCCESS and pam_acct_mgmt()==PAM_SUCCESS, each guarded by PAM_BAIL which jumps to the cleanup label leaving auth_ok at 0/-1, and auth_ok is only raised to 1 after getpwnam(), strdup(dir), initgroups() and pam_setcred() have all succeeded. No dynamic evidence obtained; PAM is also a non-default compile option."
