          "level": "none",
          "message": {
            "text": "Login-state machine bypass (ACCT, pre-auth commands, repeated USER/PASS, failed privilege drop) — Ruled out: src/ftpd.c douser/dopass/pw_check auth state machine and src/ftp_parser.c pre-auth command gate\n\nftpd.c auth flow reviewed and exercised: ACCT is answered 202 by the parser and never reaches an authentication routine (ftp_parser.c:336-340); the pre-auth command set (noop/user/acct/pass/quit/syst/auth/pbsz/prot/type/mode/feat/opts/stru/help) contains no filesystem or state-changing handler, and everything else is behind `else if (loggedin == 0) -> 530` (ftp_parser.c:453-456). dopass rejects a second PASS, an empty account, passwords >= MAX_PASSWORD_LEN, and requires auth_ok == 1 from pw_check before any of the jail/identity work; setgid/setgid and setuid/seteuid failures call _EXIT so a session can never continue with an unverified identity (ftpd.c:1801-1805, 1920-1932). Verified over FTP: USER/PASS with correct credentials reaches 230 and is chrooted to the record home (-A test: CWD/SIZE outside the jail all 550), wrong credentials give 530, and re-issued USER/PASS after login give 331/230 without changing identity."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "logicalLocations": [
                {
                  "fullyQualifiedName": "src/ftpd.c douser/dopass/pw_check auth state machine and src/ftp_parser.c pre-auth command gate"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "properties": {
