        {
          "ruleId": "strix-coverage/privilege-escalation-record-authenticating-as-uid-gid-0",
          "ruleIndex": 39,
          "kind": "pass",
          "level": "none",
          "message": {
            "text": "Privilege escalation — record authenticating as uid/gid 0 — Ruled out: src/pure-pw.c: uid/gid integer fields written into the PureDB record (useradd/usermod/show/passwd)\n\nNamed controls on every path: (1) do_useradd rejects uid/gid <= 0 unless ACCEPT_ROOT_VIRTUAL_USERS (pure-pw.c:844-848, not defined in the 1.0.54 build); (2) parse_pw_line rejects uid/gid <= 0 for existing text records (pure-pw.c:405-409); (3) usermod only overrides a fetched uid/gid when > 0 (pure-pw.c:936-941) so `-u 0`/`-u root` is a no-op; (4) the daemon-side reader re-validates with strtoul+endptr and <=0 rejection (log_puredb.c:318-336) regardless of what mkdb wrote. Verified by running the built pure-pw against a crafted passwd file: uid \"0\" lines are rejected by show/list, `-u root` is ignored by usermod. Residual (not a boundary): pure-pw's own parse uses strtoul without endptr, so \"-1\" becomes 4294967295 and is written to the DB; the daemon also accepts it (endptr consumed fully) but setuid(4294967295) fails and ftpd.c:1433/1923 exit the session, so it never yields a usable or root identity."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "logicalLocations": [
                {
                  "fullyQualifiedName": "src/pure-pw.c: uid/gid integer fields written into the PureDB record (useradd/usermod/show/passwd)"
