        {
          "ruleId": "strix-coverage/credential-db-record-injection-via-unescaped-field-separators-newlines-no-privilege-boundary",
          "ruleIndex": 40,
          "kind": "pass",
          "level": "none",
          "message": {
            "text": "Credential-DB record injection via unescaped field separators / newlines (no privilege boundary) — No issue identified: src/pure-pw.c: record serialization (login/gecos/home/ip fields) and long-line handling\n\nTested the built pure-pw (ASan+UBSan) with records containing 4090-char gecos, a >LINE_MAX line (split by fgets at pure-pw.c:520/578/1237 and re-parsed as two records), 20-colon tails and 8000-byte lines: no memory error in list/show/usermod/mkdb, every read is fgets-bounded into LINE_MAX=4096 buffers. Separator handling: filter_pw_line_sep (pure-pw.c:164-173, called for login/gecos/home at 1355/1364/1410) only maps ':' to '_'; it does NOT neutralise CR/LF. Demonstrated: `pure-pw useradd bob -c $'Bob\\nevil:...:1:1:evil:/home/evil/./:'` produced a second line in pureftpd.passwd that mkdb turned into an extra account (the ':' chars inside it became '_'). Also unfiltered: the -i/-I/-r/-R IP fields, and a newline in login or -d. This is a real record-injection/DB-corruption defect but there is no privilege boundary: every input comes from argv or from the root-owned 0600 passwd file (umask 0177 at pure-pw.c:1477, temp file O_EXCL|O_NOFOLLOW at 553-555), so only the local admin can reach it. Recommend the same guard pure-pwconvert uses (reject/escape \\r and \\n) for consistency."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "logicalLocations": [
                {
                  "fullyQualifiedName": "src/pure-pw.c: record serialization (login/gecos/home/ip fields) and long-line handling"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "properties": {
            "strix": {
              "coverage_outcome": "no_issue_found",
              "risk_area": "Credential-DB record injection via unescaped field separators / newlines (no privilege boundary)",
              "surface": "src/pure-pw.c: record serialization (login/gecos/home/ip fields) and long-line handling",
              "recorded_by": "CLI Tools And Scoreboard Auditor",
              "source": "agent_reported"
            }
          }
