        {
          "ruleId": "strix-coverage/format-string-buffer-overflow-via-long-usernames-or-filenames",
          "ruleIndex": 42,
          "kind": "pass",
          "level": "none",
          "message": {
            "text": "Format-string / buffer overflow via long usernames or filenames — No issue identified: src/altlog.c: CLF / stats / W3C / xferlog line construction\n\nNo format string use: every altlog_* builder passes a fixed format and user data as %s arguments (altlog.c:75, 219, 297, 351). Every buffer comes from ALLOCA with a size computed from the exact field lengths (strlen(host_)+strlen(account_)+strlen(quoted_filename)+fixed widths, incl. the 20-digit %llu width) and the write is wrapped in SNCHECK, which is `(CALL) >= (int)SIZE` for CONF_SNPRINTF_TYPE 8 (mysnprintf.h:27) — a failing call is dropped instead of written. urlencode (altlog.c:102-152) is length-checked at every emit. Verified with an ASan/UBSan harness driving altlog_writexfer for all four formats with a 4001-byte filename, a 127-byte account, a 2001-byte filename of regex-special '%' and an unsanitised host string: no overflow, no UB, all lines emitted whole."
          },
          "locations": [
