        {
          "ruleId": "strix-coverage/log-injection-forging-of-clf-records-from-ftp-usernames",
          "ruleIndex": 43,
          "kind": "pass",
          "level": "none",
          "message": {
            "text": "Log injection / forging of CLF records from FTP usernames — No issue identified: src/altlog.c: attacker-controlled username in log lines\n\nLog-format confusion is demonstrable but contained to one field of one line: a username is copied verbatim into `account` (ftpd.c:1293, strncpy 127 chars) and printed unescaped in the CLF/W3C/xferlog/stats user field, so `USER bob\" [1/Jan/2020:00:00:00 +0000] \"GET /spoof` produces a line with fabricated inner structure (harness output: `1.2.3.4 - bob\" [1/Jan/2020:00:00:00 +0000] \"GET /spoof [17/Nov/2026:10:16:24 -0000] \"GET /x\" 200 12345`). It cannot become a new log record: sfgets() maps every control character (incl. CR and LF) to '_' before parsing (ftp_parser.c:148-156, ISCTRLCODE in ftpd.h:768), so no \\n or \\r can reach the log. `host` is additionally sanitised to [A-Za-z0-9.:-_] by dns_sanitize() (ftpd.c:4903) and filenames are urlencoded in CLF/W3C and space/ctrl-mapped in xferlog, so neither is injectable. Net: log-field forgery by an authenticated user, no log-record injection and no other sink — observation only, not filed as a finding."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "logicalLocations": [
                {
                  "fullyQualifiedName": "src/altlog.c: attacker-controlled username in log lines"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "properties": {
            "strix": {
              "coverage_outcome": "no_issue_found",
              "risk_area": "Log injection / forging of CLF records from FTP usernames",
              "surface": "src/altlog.c: attacker-controlled username in log lines",
              "recorded_by": "CLI Tools And Scoreboard Auditor",
              "source": "agent_reported"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "ruleId": "strix-coverage/oob-read-write-when-parsing-an-attacker-supplied-stats-log",
