          "message": {
            "text": "OOB read/write when parsing an attacker-supplied stats log — Ruled out: src/pure-statsdecode.c\n\nThe only attacker-influenced surface is the file it is pointed at, and the parser is bounded: 42-byte timestamp buffer written only while `instamp < sizeof-1` (pure-statsdecode.c:54) so the terminator write at line 59 is always in range, and output is limited to non-control characters. Verified with an ASan build on a 5000-digit line, a line of 41+digits then text, embedded NUL bytes and a truncated stamp: no OOB. Running it as a root post-processing tool on a log an FTP user cannot write (altlog files are opened O_NOFOLLOW by root, ftpd.c:5069-5076) gives no privilege path."
