              "coverage_outcome": "ruled_out",
              "risk_area": "Privileged parsing of attacker-planted scoreboard files (OOB read, format string, TOCTOU)",
              "surface": "src/pure-ftpwho.c + src/ftpwho-update.c + src/ftpwho-read.c",
              "recorded_by": "CLI Tools And Scoreboard Auditor",
              "source": "agent_reported"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "ruleId": "strix-coverage/buffer-overflow-auth-bypass-on-short-or-oversized-auth-daemon-reply-with-extauth",
          "ruleIndex": 46,
          "kind": "pass",
          "level": "none",
          "message": {
            "text": "Buffer overflow / auth bypass on short or oversized auth-daemon reply (WITH_EXTAUTH) — Ruled out: src/log_extauth.c + src/pure-authd.c request/response framing\n\nNon-default build option: only compiled with --with-extauth. Request side: one 4096-byte stack buffer, snprintf wrapped in SNCHECK, so an account+password that would overflow makes the whole request be dropped and the login fails closed (log_extauth.c:213-231); account is capped at 127 bytes by ftpd.c and can contain no newline, so no field injection into the authd request. Reply side: a single safe_read capped at sizeof-1 with line[readnb]=0 (237-240), keyword matching bounded by strlen(keyword) (248-254), and the result is forced to failure unless the daemon sent the end marker AND uid>0 AND gid>0 AND an absolute dir (258-263) — a short, truncated or oversized reply therefore denies rather than authenticates. pure-authd mirrors the pattern (4095-byte buffer, ended marker required, child _exit(EXIT_FAILURE) otherwise, pure-authd.c:288-340) and its socket is created 0600 with the path length checked against sun_path (354-392). No unchecked copies: the only memcpy uses are the sun_path copies, sized strlen+1 into a malloc(strlen+1+sizeof) block. Nothing here is reachable by an FTP client beyond the two credential strings."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "logicalLocations": [
                {
                  "fullyQualifiedName": "src/log_extauth.c + src/pure-authd.c request/response framing"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "properties": {
            "strix": {
