            }
          }
        },
        {
          "ruleId": "strix-coverage/stored-xss-output-injection-in-the-cgi-status-page-via-attacker-controlled-session-fields",
          "ruleIndex": 48,
          "kind": "pass",
          "level": "none",
          "message": {
            "text": "Stored XSS / output-injection in the CGI status page via attacker-controlled session fields — Ruled out: src/pure-ftpwho.c HTML/XML/plist/shell output\n\npure-ftpwho is commonly deployed as a CGI (-c / GATEWAY_INTERFACE) that renders the account, filename and peer host of live sessions — all attacker-influenced. Every one of those fields is passed through html_escaped()/xml_escaped() (pure-ftpwho.c:214-271, 344-403, 460-510), which entity-encodes &, <, > and \" with bounds-checked output (left < sizeof \"&quot;\"-1 etc.), and the numeric fields use %lu. No unescaped user data reaches the HTML/XML/plist/shell writers; the shell writer additionally escapes | and \\ and maps control characters (pure-ftpwho.c:592-620). No XSS/format-string path from a session's filename or login into the status page."
          },
          "locations": [
