        {
          "ruleId": "strix-coverage/ftp-bounce-privileged-port-connection-via-active-mode",
          "ruleIndex": 49,
          "kind": "pass",
          "level": "none",
          "message": {
            "text": "FTP bounce / privileged-port connection via active mode — Ruled out: PORT and EPRT client port-range enforcement (IPv4 PORT, IPv4/IPv6 EPRT, PASV/EPSV)\n\nNamed control: doport2() (src/ftpd.c) rejects any port below 1024 with 501 MSG_BAD_PORT, and that function is the single entry point for both PORT and EPRT (IPv4 branch and do_ipv6_port both end in doport2()). The parsers additionally reject port 0 and >65535 (doeprt: `port > 65535U || port <= 0U` after atoi; do_ipv6_port: strtoul with endptr==delimiter and `port <= 0 || port > 65535`). Verified live: PORT 127,0,0,1,0,21 and EPRT |1|...|1| return 501 \"won't connect to ports < 1024\"; ports 0, 65536, 99999, -1 and huge decimal strings return 501 syntax error; 1024/65535 are accepted. PASV/EPSV expose only server-chosen ports from firstport..lastport."
          },
