        {
          "ruleId": "strix-coverage/memory-safety-stack-heap-overflow-off-by-one-oob-read-on-command-lines-and-arguments",
          "ruleIndex": 50,
          "kind": "pass",
          "level": "none",
          "message": {
            "text": "Memory safety: stack/heap overflow, off-by-one, OOB read on command lines and arguments — Ruled out: src/ftp_parser.c command tokeniser and line reader (sfgets/parser/revealextraspc/sfgets pipelining)\n\nEvery read/write is bounded by the command buffer and length control declared in src/globals.h (cmdsize = PATH_MAX + 16, cmd[PATH_MAX + 32]); sfgets refuses to scan past cmdsize and calls die(421, MSG_LINE_TOO_LONG) when no newline is found, and it always leaves a NUL inside the buffer, so the parser's `while (isalnum(cmd[n]) && n < cmdsize)` loop and the `n >= cmdsize` guard cannot run off the buffer. Verified dynamically under an AddressSanitizer build (-fsanitize=address) with boundary lines of 4110/4111/4112/4113/4200/9000 bytes, pipelined commands, bare LF/CRLF and 850+ randomised malformed command iterations: no ASAN reports, and 4110 bytes is accepted while 4111+ returns 421 Line too long."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "logicalLocations": [
                {
                  "fullyQualifiedName": "src/ftp_parser.c command tokeniser and line reader (sfgets/parser/revealextraspc/sfgets pipelining)"
                }
