          "message": {
            "text": "Numeric/date parsing: unchecked atoi/strtoul, out-of-range values, length used for allocation — No issue identified: SIZE/MDTM/MFMT/SITE UTIME date parsing and REST/ALLO numeric parsing (src/ftpd.c, src/ftp_parser.c)\n\ndoutime parses with bounded sscanf widths (%4d%2d%2d%2d%2d%2d) into a zeroed struct tm and rejects tm_mon<0, tm_year<=0 and ts==(time_t)-1; dorest/doallo use strtoull with endptr plus a negative off_t check, and no parse result is ever used as an allocation size. Verified live with empty, short, overflowing (18446744073709551616), negative, out-of-range (month 99, year 99999999999999999999) and garbage arguments: all rejected with 501/554 and no crash under ASAN."
