          "ruleId": "strix-coverage/sub-parser-argument-handling-buffer-overflows-unchecked-conversions-malformed-token-splitting",
          "ruleIndex": 54,
          "kind": "pass",
          "level": "none",
          "message": {
            "text": "Sub-parser argument handling: buffer overflows, unchecked conversions, malformed token splitting — No issue identified: SITE sub-parsers (CHMOD/IDLE/UTIME/HELP/ALIAS) and OPTS/TYPE/MODE/STRU handlers (src/ftp_parser.c)\n\nSITE CHMOD parses the mode with strtoul(base 8) and rejects values above 07777 (including -1 and 21-digit strings, which saturate), SITE IDLE uses strtoul with endptr garbage detection and caps at MAX_SITE_IDLE (2520), SITE UTIME requires the RFC 3659 five-token form and splits it with bounded strrchr pointer walks that always terminate on the argument string itself, SITE HELP/ALIAS only compare strings, and OPTS/MLST truncates its reply from a constant. Verified live with malformed, negative, overflowing and truncated arguments for each: correct 501/550 replies, no crash under ASAN."
          },
