              "surface": "PureDB IPv4 allow/deny rule evaluation (src/log_puredb.c access_ip_check/access_ip_match)",
              "recorded_by": "Protocol And IP Rule Auditor",
              "source": "agent_reported"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "ruleId": "strix-coverage/fail-open-on-malformed-cidr-widths-mask-underflow-ub-shift",
          "ruleIndex": 56,
          "kind": "pass",
          "level": "none",
          "message": {
            "text": "Fail-open on malformed CIDR widths (mask underflow/UB shift) — Ruled out: Malformed CIDR width handling in access_ip_match (IPv4 mask maths, IPv6 prefix parsing)\n\nNamed control: access_ip_match() rejects IPv4 widths with netbits==0 or >32 and IPv6 prefixes that are 0, >128 or non-numeric by returning -1 after logging the offending pattern, and every caller in access_ip_check() maps -1 to \"denied\" (allow-only returns -1, deny-only treats non-zero as denied, both-lists requires allow==1 and deny==0). Verified live: allow rule 127.0.0.1/33 and 127.0.0.0/0 both deny the client, deny rule 127.0.0.1/33 denies, and a /129 IPv6 prefix is rejected for IPv6 clients. No wrap-around or `>> 32` shift is reachable because the width is range-checked before the mask computation."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "logicalLocations": [
                {
                  "fullyQualifiedName": "Malformed CIDR width handling in access_ip_match (IPv4 mask maths, IPv6 prefix parsing)"
