          "kind": "pass",
          "level": "none",
          "message": {
            "text": "Deny-rule bypass by address representation (IPv4-mapped IPv6, zone-id, leading zeros) — Ruled out: Client address normalisation before rule evaluation (fourinsix/checkvalidaddr in src/ftpd.c doit)\n\nNamed control: fourinsix() in src/ftpd.c converts AF_INET6 source addresses that are IPv4-mapped into AF_INET, and doit() applies it to both ctrlconn and peer before any authentication (and again to accepted data connections). Verified live: a client connecting to ::ffff:127.0.0.1 is matched by an IPv4 deny rule (127.0.0.1/32 denies it) rather than escaping it, and an IPv4 rule does not match a genuine ::1 client, which is the documented per-family behaviour an operator must cover explicitly."
          },
